  "content": {
    "id": "v2-8731d-p23-practice-slot-10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Three shearers take 4 days to shear a flock of 240 sheep.\nA farmer has 600 sheep to shear.\nShe hires 5 shearers and pays each of them $\\$190$ per day.\nHow much will it cost her to shear all of her sheep?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$5700$",
      "worked": "The flock is $600\\div240=2.5$ times the size, so 3 shearers would take $4\\times2.5=10$ days. Let $t$ be the time in days and $N$ the number of shearers for the whole flock.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}t&=\\frac{k}{N}\\\\10&=\\frac{k}{3}\\\\k&=30\\\\t&=\\frac{30}{N}=\\frac{30}{5}=6\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe total cost is\n\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=5\\times6\\times190\\\\C&=5700.\\end{align*}$$\n\nIt will cost $\\$5700$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
